.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt DISK-AGENT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm disk-agent
.Nd SMART and ZFS pool state for Home Assistant
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Cm key add Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Cm key list
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Cm key remove Ar id
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility serves the SMART state of every disk and the state of every ZFS
pool of its host as JSON over HTTP for the ha_disk_monitor Home Assistant
integration to poll. It is a single Go binary intended to run under systemd
on Debian and under SMF on OmniOS.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl -config Ar dir"
.It Fl -config Ar dir
Read the configuration files from the directory
.Ar dir
instead of
.Ev CONFIG_DIR
or the per-user default location.
.It Fl -version
Print the application version and exit.
.It Cm key add Ar name
Make an API key named
.Ar name ,
print it once and store its hash in
.Pa keys.json
beside the configuration files.
.It Cm key list
List the API keys with their ids.
.It Cm key remove Ar id
Delete the API key with that id.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a directory of two files:
.Pa app.config.yaml
and
.Pa auth.config.yaml .
The packaged service uses
.Pa /etc/disk-agent/ ,
where the package seeds them.
.Pp
See
.Xr disk-agent.yaml 5
for the configuration file format.
.Sh SERVICE MANAGEMENT
On Debian the service is managed through systemd:
.Pp
.Dl # systemctl enable --now disk-agent
.Dl # systemctl disable disk-agent
.Dl # systemctl restart disk-agent
.Dl # systemctl status disk-agent
.Pp
On OmniOS the service is managed through SMF:
.Pp
.Dl # svcadm enable system/monitoring/disk-agent
.Dl # svcadm disable system/monitoring/disk-agent
.Dl # svcs -l system/monitoring/disk-agent
.Sh API ENDPOINTS
The public identity and capability probe:
.Pp
.Dl http://0.0.0.0:9430/api/status
.Pp
Behind an API key, the current report and the stream the Home Assistant
integration holds open:
.Pp
.Dl GET /api/report
.Dl GET /api/disks
.Dl GET /api/pools
.Dl GET /api/events
.Pp
No request collects anything. The host's own daemons refresh the report
through the trigger socket beside the configuration files: ZED and
syseventd on every ZFS event, smartd on every SMART warning, udev and the
device sysevents on hot plug. Every refresh is written to each open
.Pa /api/events
stream.
.Pp
With
.Cm ssl.enabled
the same surface is served over HTTPS on
.Cm server.https_port
(default 9431). Every route lives under
.Pa /api .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /etc/disk-agent/<name>.config.yaml"
.It Pa /usr/bin/disk-agent
The agent binary on Debian
.It Pa /opt/disk-agent/disk-agent
The agent binary on OmniOS
.It Pa /etc/disk-agent/<name>.config.yaml
Configuration files (app, auth)
.It Pa /usr/share/disk-agent/config/<name>.config.yaml
The seed files the Debian package installs and postinst copies into place
.It Pa /var/log/disk-agent/
Service log directory
.It Pa /var/lib/disk-agent/
Service data directory
.It Pa /etc/systemd/system/disk-agent.service
Systemd service unit
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground for testing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ disk-agent --config /etc/disk-agent
.Ed
.Pp
Check the agent is up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl http://127.0.0.1:9430/api/status
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The agent logs to a rotating text log file (see
.Xr disk-agent.yaml 5 )
and, when a console is attached, to standard error. Under systemd, console
output is captured by the journal:
.Pp
.Dl # journalctl -u disk-agent
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr disk-agent.yaml 5 ,
.Xr systemctl 1 ,
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr svcadm 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Makr91
.Sh SECURITY
Every route under
.Pa /api
other than the public status and health probes requires an API key made with
.Cm key add .
Keep the configuration directory's filesystem permissions restrictive.
